1
00:00:08,748 --> 00:00:11,349
A painful feeling is the first arrow.

2
00:00:11,429 --> 00:00:13,446
What we do with it is the second.

3
00:00:14,248 --> 00:00:16,876
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

4
00:00:16,956 --> 00:00:20,834
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

5
00:00:21,644 --> 00:00:25,509
Part 1 set out the twelve links, and
traced them through one afternoon.

6
00:00:25,589 --> 00:00:29,680
Part 2 asked who goes round the wheel,
and found the tradition's answer.

7
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,242
Not a valid question.

8
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:35,364
Karma and rebirth kept, and no
one in the chain who goes round.

9
00:00:36,168 --> 00:00:38,361
The twelve links come in two orders.

10
00:00:38,441 --> 00:00:41,174
So far I have mostly followed the first.

11
00:00:41,254 --> 00:00:42,845
Here I take up the second.

12
00:00:42,925 --> 00:00:45,970
How the chain stops, in
the tradition's own terms.

13
00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:48,488
This part closes Section 5.

14
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,662
The discourses give it as
plainly as the forward order.

15
00:00:52,742 --> 00:00:56,670
With the fading away and ending
of ignorance, formations end.

16
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:59,741
With the ending of formations,
consciousness ends.

17
00:00:59,821 --> 00:01:01,480
And so on, to the end.

18
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:04,365
Such is the ending of this
whole mass of suffering.

19
00:01:05,168 --> 00:01:08,267
So the chain does not have
to be broken link by link,

20
00:01:08,347 --> 00:01:11,161
as if one had to defeat
birth, then becoming,

21
00:01:11,241 --> 00:01:13,272
then clinging, each in turn.

22
00:01:13,352 --> 00:01:15,745
Each link stands only on its condition.

23
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:19,576
Remove the condition, and what
stood on it does not arise.

24
00:01:19,656 --> 00:01:21,931
When this is not, that is not.

25
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:26,537
The tradition points to two
places where the chain can be met.

26
00:01:27,352 --> 00:01:29,410
At the start, ignorance.

27
00:01:29,489 --> 00:01:34,410
In the discourses, ignorance is
defined exactly. Not knowing suffering.

28
00:01:34,489 --> 00:01:37,670
Not knowing its arising.
Not knowing its ending.

29
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:39,491
Not knowing the way to its ending.

30
00:01:39,571 --> 00:01:41,679
So it ends by knowing those four.

31
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:43,626
This is the work of insight.

32
00:01:44,420 --> 00:01:46,831
And in the middle, feeling and craving.

33
00:01:46,911 --> 00:01:48,597
Contact brings feeling.

34
00:01:48,677 --> 00:01:53,583
Feeling is followed by craving. More
of the pleasant. An end to the painful.

35
00:01:53,663 --> 00:01:56,790
Then clinging, and then a
whole world built around it.

36
00:01:56,870 --> 00:01:59,181
This is one of the three
joints of the chain.

37
00:01:59,261 --> 00:02:02,053
The point where what is met
turns into what is done.

38
00:02:02,856 --> 00:02:05,321
I see these as two sides of one cut.

39
00:02:05,401 --> 00:02:09,193
In the middle, the step from feeling to
craving is where the chain shows itself

40
00:02:09,273 --> 00:02:13,446
most clearly. At the start,
knowing what that step really is,

41
00:02:13,526 --> 00:02:16,562
and that it leads to
suffering, is what lets it go.

42
00:02:17,356 --> 00:02:19,549
The Buddha gives an image for the middle.

43
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:25,475
When an untaught person is touched by a
painful feeling, they grieve. They lament.

44
00:02:25,555 --> 00:02:28,790
They feel two pains, the
bodily and the mental.

45
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:32,762
It is as if they were struck by
one arrow, and then by a second.

46
00:02:33,564 --> 00:02:37,809
When a taught disciple is touched by
a painful feeling, they feel one pain.

47
00:02:37,889 --> 00:02:40,336
The bodily one, and not the mental.

48
00:02:40,416 --> 00:02:44,199
Struck by the first arrow, they
are not struck by the second.

49
00:02:45,016 --> 00:02:46,965
Notice what this does not say.

50
00:02:47,045 --> 00:02:49,465
It does not say the wise feel no pain.

51
00:02:49,545 --> 00:02:51,612
The first arrow still lands.

52
00:02:51,692 --> 00:02:55,987
What ends is the second arrow.
The craving. The pushing away.

53
00:02:56,067 --> 00:02:58,178
The story of the one who was hurt.

54
00:02:58,988 --> 00:03:00,869
So the cut is not numbness.

55
00:03:00,949 --> 00:03:03,776
One can try to stop
feeling, to dull the senses,

56
00:03:03,856 --> 00:03:05,407
to stay above the world.

57
00:03:05,487 --> 00:03:07,404
That is not the reverse order.

58
00:03:07,484 --> 00:03:10,230
The reverse order leaves the world vivid.

59
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:13,006
And removes only what
was being added to it.

60
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:17,338
How does ignorance end? In
the discourses, by seeing.

61
00:03:17,418 --> 00:03:20,491
Seeing the arising and
passing away of body,

62
00:03:20,571 --> 00:03:24,105
feeling, perception,
formations and consciousness.

63
00:03:24,185 --> 00:03:25,790
Again and again.

64
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:30,368
Until it is plain that what arises
and passes cannot be held as mine,

65
00:03:30,448 --> 00:03:32,180
or I, or my self.

66
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:35,676
That has a consequence
I want to state plainly.

67
00:03:35,756 --> 00:03:38,384
Ignorance does not end
by stopping thought.

68
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:42,508
A quiet, wordless mind
can be very pleasant.

69
00:03:42,588 --> 00:03:46,203
The tradition values it highly,
as the ground for insight.

70
00:03:46,283 --> 00:03:47,983
But thought is not the problem.

71
00:03:48,063 --> 00:03:49,722
The habit of fixing is.

72
00:03:49,802 --> 00:03:55,429
Taking what appears to stand on its
own. The speaker. The words. The hurt.

73
00:03:55,509 --> 00:03:56,724
The one hurt.

74
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:00,915
A quiet mind does not end
that habit by being quiet.

75
00:04:00,995 --> 00:04:04,761
When thinking starts again, the
habit is still there, waiting.

76
00:04:04,841 --> 00:04:06,300
What ends it is seeing.

77
00:04:07,096 --> 00:04:09,819
Such is the ending of this
whole mass of suffering.

78
00:04:09,899 --> 00:04:12,537
It is easy to hear this
as the end of everything.

79
00:04:12,617 --> 00:04:16,169
No more feeling, no more world, a blank.

80
00:04:16,964 --> 00:04:19,144
The discourses do not say that.

81
00:04:19,224 --> 00:04:23,587
The one who has seen through still
sees, still hears, still feels.

82
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:25,829
The second arrow is what has gone.

83
00:04:25,909 --> 00:04:30,666
Asked what nirvāṇa is, one monk
answers simply. The ending of becoming.

84
00:04:30,746 --> 00:04:33,057
What ends is the taking on of an identity,

85
00:04:33,137 --> 00:04:35,000
to be defended and renewed.

86
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,970
Not the bell ringing when struck.

87
00:04:37,050 --> 00:04:38,904
Not the seed giving rice.

88
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:43,186
And when a wanderer asks where
the awakened one goes after death,

89
00:04:43,266 --> 00:04:45,419
the Buddha asks him a question back.

90
00:04:45,499 --> 00:04:48,544
When a fire goes out, in
which direction has it gone?

91
00:04:48,624 --> 00:04:51,261
East, west, north or south?

92
00:04:51,341 --> 00:04:53,938
It does not apply, the wanderer says.

93
00:04:54,018 --> 00:04:56,442
It went out because its fuel was used up.

94
00:04:57,244 --> 00:05:00,674
The ending of suffering is
not a thing being destroyed.

95
00:05:00,754 --> 00:05:02,798
And not someone going somewhere.

96
00:05:03,608 --> 00:05:06,055
There is one more teaching
I want to include,

97
00:05:06,135 --> 00:05:08,098
because it is easily forgotten.

98
00:05:08,916 --> 00:05:11,825
In one discourse, the
Buddha gives the chain,

99
00:05:11,905 --> 00:05:13,990
and then keeps going past suffering.

100
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:16,816
With suffering as
condition, there is faith.

101
00:05:16,896 --> 00:05:18,840
With faith, gladness.

102
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,903
Then joy, calm, happiness,
and a settled mind.

103
00:05:22,983 --> 00:05:24,724
Then seeing things as they are.

104
00:05:24,804 --> 00:05:27,934
Then turning away,
letting go, and freedom.

105
00:05:28,744 --> 00:05:31,100
The same sentence runs both ways.

106
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:34,850
When this is, that is,
describes how suffering builds.

107
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:36,902
And also how freedom builds.

108
00:05:36,982 --> 00:05:39,932
The path is not outside dependent arising.

109
00:05:40,012 --> 00:05:43,279
It is dependent arising,
arranged the other way.

110
00:05:44,084 --> 00:05:46,318
Return to the afternoon of Part 1.

111
00:05:46,398 --> 00:05:48,863
Someone says something
harsh to me at work.

112
00:05:49,656 --> 00:05:53,969
There is contact. The words,
the ear, the knowing of them.

113
00:05:54,049 --> 00:05:56,646
There is feeling, unpleasant and sharp.

114
00:05:56,726 --> 00:05:59,594
The first arrow lands, and that is fine.

115
00:05:59,674 --> 00:06:02,542
Then the familiar pull
begins, toward an apology,

116
00:06:02,622 --> 00:06:04,232
toward being shown right.

117
00:06:05,044 --> 00:06:10,756
But this time it is seen. Not suppressed.
Not argued with. Seen as what it is.

118
00:06:10,836 --> 00:06:13,039
A feeling arising and passing.

119
00:06:13,119 --> 00:06:15,294
A pull arising and passing.

120
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:17,024
With no owner among them.

121
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:21,283
The pull does not find
much to hold. No clinging.

122
00:06:21,363 --> 00:06:23,498
No injured party taking shape.

123
00:06:23,578 --> 00:06:26,587
No grievance born, to
be rehearsed in the car.

124
00:06:27,396 --> 00:06:29,155
The words were still heard.

125
00:06:29,235 --> 00:06:31,098
The feeling was still felt.

126
00:06:31,178 --> 00:06:33,412
Nothing was taken from the afternoon.

127
00:06:34,216 --> 00:06:38,321
This is Section 5, Part 3 of
the Dependent Arising series,

128
00:06:38,401 --> 00:06:40,431
and the close of Section 5.

129
00:06:41,228 --> 00:06:45,174
What changed is only that the chain
was watched, instead of obeyed.

